%% How a taskRef becomes a running step — Pipelines Fundamentals, lab exercise 2 and concept
%% "Three reuse layers". The Pipeline step holds only a reference (resolver: cluster, plus a Task
%% name and namespace); when a run starts, the cluster resolver fetches that Task from the shared
%% library namespace, and the step runs on the image that Task names. Fix the Task once and every
%% pipeline picks the fix up on its next run.
%% Shape (diagram-size-guard): LR, chain of 4, no subgraph, labels at most 2 lines.
flowchart LR
  REF["unit-test step<br/>taskRef: resolver cluster"] -->|"run starts"| RES["cluster resolver"]
  RES -->|"name + namespace"| LIB[("ogsr-parasol-tasks<br/>maven-jdk21")]
  LIB -->|"Task spec"| POD["unit-test Pod<br/>openjdk-21 image"]
  classDef hi fill:#e00,stroke:#900,color:#fff;
  classDef lib fill:#fef5e7,stroke:#b7791f,color:#744210;
  classDef done fill:#e6f4ea,stroke:#137333,color:#0d652d;
  class RES hi;
  class LIB lib;
  class POD done;
